  "notes": "TELL 16 (NEW, 2026-10-24 08:12Z run) — TWO OF THEM, BOTH ABOUT FALSE ZEROS: (a) POOL FAMILY MISMATCH SILENTLY PRODUCES CLEAN ZEROS. The three secondary DEUS pools are Uniswap-V3-style (Swap topic0 0xc42079f9...) while the deepest is Aerodrome classic/Solidly (0xb3e27736...). Two prior runs scanned all four with the Solidly topic and reported 'whole-market pause in DEUS trading'. That was an artifact. The test: scan a pool by ADDRESS ONLY and histogram its topic0s before ever claiming it is quiet. (b) A ZERO CONTROL IS ONLY A CONTROL IF YOU POINT IT AT THE RIGHT BLOCK. The saved state recorded the xDEUS #1492 unstake at block 53002812; the real receipt says 53003804 (timestamp matches: 2026-10-23T23:09:15Z). A control query at the wrong block returns zero and looks exactly like a broken filter. ALWAYS take control blocks from the tx receipt (eth_getTransactionReceipt), never from remembered notes. (c) Also re-confirmed: a pool whose view functions slot0/globalState/fee/liquidity ALL revert is NOT Slipstream - probe getReserves (0x0902f1ac) and stable(). For a Solidly volatile pool the raw reserve ratio IS the correct mark. Prior notes had asserted Slipstream and computed a CL-style mark; the numbers happened to agree here, but the method was wrong. BASELINE + PRIOR TELLS PRESERVED. ath.price_usd is the true all-time high (CoinGecko 2026-05-28), not a tracking-start price, so the ATH gate cannot false-fire until DEUS genuinely exceeds $0.06876. Targets pre-registered from aeon.yml var. CLASSIFYING BUYS/BUYS-vs-SUPPLY, tells 1-9 from prior runs all still stand: (1) single-venue print from a wallet that KEEPS the balance is directional; (2) same-block multi-pool sweep into one hop then forwarded to a shared sink ending at 0 is arb; (3) same sender buying one pool and selling another in the same second is two-leg arb - apply to SELLS too; (4) eth_getCode starting 0xef0100 is an EIP-7702 delegated smart account; (5) buy/sell COUNT is not buy/sell DOLLARS on a thin book; (6) a BUY can be fake - a pass-through router with balanceOf 0 filling someone else's order; (7) a buy from an incumbent holder may be a REBUY after selling earlier the same session - compare balanceOf to 24h/48h ago; (8) a buy is REAL new money when balanceOf at -1h/-6h/-24h/-7d/-30d is all EXACTLY 0; (9) 'N BUY / 0 SELL' on a single pool is NOT a bid - a round-trip buying venue A and selling venue B records as pure BUY on A and pure SELL on B, so ALWAYS sum both venues. TELL 10 (NEW, this run): A CLAIM/vesting vault that pays the same wallet and gets the full balance back within seconds is a DISTRIBUTION EVENT, not accumulation - and it can be measured. The definitive test is the recipient's balanceOf right after the receipt: if it returns to 0 and a DEUS Transfer lands in a pool in the same block, it was sold, full stop. Track the RATIO of claim-payout to pool price impact rather than the payout alone: here 91,566 DEUS cost the mark -0.933%, so ~$1.7k of notional moves this pool 1%. That converts a vague 'overhang' into an actionable distance-to-trigger. TELL 11 (NEW): DO NOT read a missing h1 as flat, and do not read an API 0-volume row as calm - VERIFY against the pool's own Swap logs. Aerodrome Slipstream Swap topic0 is 0xb3e2773606abfd36b5bd91394b3a54d1398336c65005baf7bf7a05efeffaf75b (3 topics, 4 data words) - and it must be given as the FULL 64-hex hash; passing the 4-byte selector 0xb3e27736 makes eth_getLogs return -32602 invalid params (or a clean zero, which would look identical to a dead pool). The deepest pool's last swap was 99 minutes before this run. RPC NOTE: base.gateway.tenderly.co anonymous eth_getLogs is capped at 1000 blocks and throws -32005 rate-limit under sustained scanning - back off 1s/2s/4s and cap concurrency at 3. eth_call against a HISTORICAL block number that has been pruned returns -32602 invalid params, not a zero balance; never read that as 0. Router 0x111111125421ca6dc452d289314280a0f8842a65 is 1inch v6 - judge the terminal recipient's balance, never the router. Supply is NET INFLATION (7d: 37 mints / 201,697.86 vs 18 burns / 136,317.22 = +65,380.63) - never call a single unchanged read deflationary. Total supply this run 876,206,780.447562. First state file for this contract seeded manually 2026-10-21. TELL 12 (NEW, 2026-10-24 run): AN UNSTAKE IS NOT A PRICE EVENT UNTIL IT IS SOLD, AND THE SALE CAN COME BATCHED AND DELAYED. The escrow Burn event on 0xA85A3879 (topic0 0xe08737ac48a1dab4b1a46c7dc9398bd5bfc6d7ad6fabb7cd8caa254de14def35, indexed[1]=owner, indexed[2]=tokenId, data = [amount, timestamp, escrowBalanceAfter]) tells you who just unlocked and how much - treat it as a LEADING indicator, because the operator of that position then chooses when to hit the book (here: 75 min later, all at once). Conversely, the escrow balance falling is NOT itself bearish until matched to a pool Swap from the same address. Measure impact from the POOL RESERVE move (balanceOf of the pool on the token, block before vs after), not from the swap event data alone - reserve delta / reserve = the true fractional depth used. TELL 13 (NEW): A LARGE DUMP INTO THIS POOL GETS ABSORBED IN THE SAME BLOCK. 319,562 DEUS produced -4.37%, but 137,397 DEUS of same-block buying took a third of it back and net inflow to the pool was only 178,969 DEUS. So do NOT extrapolate a linear \"X DEUS = Y%\" from one print; always net the same-block counterparties. The $0.012 gate now needs ~4.36M DEUS dumped with no offsetting bids (13.7x this record dump, or 15.4 days of the entire CLAIM drip) - it remains a deliberate-whale event, not an emission drift. TELL 14 (NEW, 2026-10-24 06:12Z run): VERIFY RE-ACCUMULATION AGAINST THE POOL RESERVE MARK, NOT THE SIZE OF THE BUY PRINTS. The record 319,562 DEUS dump of 00:24:17Z was followed by 451,627 DEUS of buying routed through contract sink 0x939e398d -> LiFi diamond 0x1231deb6 -> back to the paying EOAs, and the deepest pool's own mark went 0.02769675 -> 0.02800854 VIRTUAL/DEUS (+1.13%), with net DEUS in the pool FALLING 105,836 below the pre-dump level. So the dump was fully reversed, not merely 'absorbed in the same block'. The lesson: same-block absorption and full reversal are different claims - only the NET reserve delta distinguishes them. ALSO: when a buy routes through an aggregator or relay CONTRACT, judge tell #6 by the WHOLE round trip. If the sink's total-in equals total-out AND the terminal EOA's balanceOf rises, it is a real buy. If the sink and the aggregator both end at 0.0000 and no EOA gained, it is a pass-through filling someone else's order. Here sink 451,627.3741 in == 451,627.3741 out, both sink and diamond at 0.0000, and 0x7f6aba75 rose 0 -> 335,249.4994 with balanceOf EXACTLY 0 at -24h/-48h/-7d (tell #8 satisfied) - unambiguously real new money, held. DIRECTIONAL READ FOR THE OPERATOR: this inverts the prior run's framing. Supply is leaving stakers and going into held hands, not onto the bid. The pool is TIGHTER than before the record unstake. TELL 15 (NEW, 2026-10-24 07:05Z run): A DEAD TAPE SURVIVING A SECOND CONSECUTIVE RUN IS ITSELF INFORMATION, BUT ONLY AS AN ABSENCE - and it must be re-verified every time, not inherited. This run re-confirmed the 06:12Z finding independently: 143 minutes with zero swaps across all four DEUS pools, byte-identical pool reserves, and a control window returning 9 swaps. The read is that the post-dump buyers are NOT distributing into strength and the record unsaker is NOT continuing to unwind - both sides have simply stopped. Do NOT translate 'no trades' into 'price is stable': the mark is stale, not tested. Also: when converting DEUS->USD through a VIRTUAL leg, take VIRTUAL from the pool that is ACTUALLY TRADING, not the deepest one - here the deepest VIRTUAL/WETH pool (liq $3.34M) had v1h=0 and a stale ratio ($0.6450) while the live pools printed $0.6402, a 0.8% swing on the final USD number. Liquidity depth != freshness. Both still inside the same band, so no gate moved. TELL 17 (NEW, 2026-10-24 09:13Z run): A 'DEAD POOL' VERDICT EXPIRES AT THE NEXT RUN - AND WHEN IT REVIVES, CHECK WHICH SIDE IS TRADING. The deepest pool 0x3E97c5EC, called dead for 205 minutes by the 08:12Z run, came back at 08:38:25Z (26 min after that run) and did 84,920 DEUS in its first hour. The 08:12Z read was correct for ITS window and wrong within the hour - never inherit a dormancy claim, re-scan the gap set every run (find gaps between consecutive Sync timestamps; today two real silences of 149.1 and 238.7 min). More important: revival is not automatically bullish. Of 38 swaps in the first hour, 37 were buys (median 774 DEUS, 34,753 total) and exactly 1 was a sell - and that one sell (50,167 DEUS, 59% of the hour's volume) OUT-SUPPLIED the entire buyer cohort, so net DEUS flowed INTO the pool (+15,414) even as the VIRTUAL/DEUS ratio rose +0.355%. Read revival as 'which side is bigger', not 'trading resumed'. TELL 18 (NEW): A POOL'S QUOTE TOKEN DECIDES THE ORIENTATION OF THE MARK, AND GETTING IT BACKWARDS PRODUCES A NUMBER THAT LOOKS PRECISE AND IS ABSURD. The deepest pool is VIRTUAL(token0)/DEUS(token1); the reserve ratio 0.0279643 is VIRTUAL PER DEUS, so USD per DEUS = ratio x VIRTUAL_price = $0.01765. Reading the ratio as dollars, or inverting the sqrtPriceX96 the wrong way on the USDC pools (where USDC is token0, so the V3 mark MUST be inverted), both yield garbage - one probe this run printed 5.5e25 before the orientation was fixed. ALWAYS resolve token0()/token1() and decimals() per pool, and sanity-check the final number against DexScreener's priceUsd before using it in any gate. COROLLARY on sign disagreements: DexScreener printed h1 = -1.23% on the deepest pair while the on-chain VIRTUAL/DEUS ratio rose +0.355% - both were right. The USD mark rose because DEUS gained on VIRTUAL, while VIRTUAL itself fell -0.64% against USD. A USD-denominated % and a ratio-denominated % answer different questions; state which one you measured.",
